**Assignment No. 3: Color to Grayscale and Binary** 

**Problem Statement:** Convert a given colour image into grayscale and then into black & white. 

### **Algorithm Highlights**

* 
**Color to Gray:** Uses a linear combination of R, G, and B channels: $f(x,y) = 0.299 \cdot R + 0.587 \cdot G + 0.114 \cdot B$. 


* 
**Gray to Binary:** Uses thresholding to obtain a black and white image. 



**Code** 

```scilab
img = imread("./assets/color_rose.jpg");
figure(0);
subplot(1, 3, 1); title("Color Image"); imshow(img);
gray_img = rgb2gray(img);
subplot(1, 3, 2); title("Gray Scale Image"); imshow(gray_img);
bw_img = im2bw(gray_img, 0.3);
subplot(1, 3, 3); title("Binary Image"); imshow(bw_img);

```



